  "二、 算路引擎优化：PRC 与 iSPF 的分工协作": "II. Path Calculation Engine Optimization: Division of Labor between PRC and iSPF",
  "传统 SPF 算法把全网当成一个整体。拓扑中有任意节点或链路变化，算法都会推倒整棵最短路径树（SPT）并重新遍历计算所有节点，计算复杂度高达": "Traditional SPF algorithms treat the entire network as a single entity. If any node or link in the topology changes, the algorithm discards the entire Shortest Path Tree (SPT) and re-traverses all nodes, resulting in high computational complexity.",
  "现代 OSPF 将网络解构为两层：": "Modern OSPF deconstructs the network into two layers:",
  "节点（Node/Router）": "Node/Router",
  "构成拓扑骨架树（SPT），": "Forms the topological backbone tree (SPT),",
  "叶子（Leaf/Prefix）": "Leaf/Prefix",
  "挂载在节点上代表具体的业务路由。": "Attached to nodes to represent specific service routes.",
  "flowchart TD\n    Change[\"网络发生变动\"] --> Check{\"是节点拓扑变化，<br/>还是仅路由前缀变化？\"}\n    \n    Check -- \"骨干拓扑改变 (邻居UP/DOWN)\" --> iSPF[\"【 iSPF 增量计算 】<br/>只重新计算受影响的子树节点<br/>(保留稳定树干，大幅省 CPU)\"]\n    Check -- \"叶子路由改变 (接口使能/Loopback)\" --> PRC[\"【 PRC 部分路由计算 】<br/>SPT 拓扑树完全不动<br/>只针对变动的叶子前缀做更新\"]\n\n    style iSPF fill:#ffebe9,stroke:#cf222e,stroke-width:1px\n    style PRC fill:#dafbe1,stroke:#1a7f37,stroke-width:1px": "flowchart TD\n    Change[\"Network change occurs\"] --> Check{\"Is it a node topology change, <br/>or just a route prefix change?\"}\n    \n    Check -- \"Backbone topology change (Neighbor UP/DOWN)\" --> iSPF[\"【 iSPF Incremental Calculation 】<br/>Only recalculates affected subtree nodes<br/>(Retains stable trunk, significantly saves CPU)\"]\n    Check -- \"Leaf route change (Interface enable/Loopback)\" --> PRC[\"【 PRC Partial Route Calculation 】<br/>SPT topology tree remains untouched<br/>Only updates the changed leaf prefixes\"]\n\n    style iSPF fill:#ffebe9,stroke:#cf222e,stroke-width:1px\n    style PRC fill:#dafbe1,stroke:#1a7f37,stroke-width:1px",
  "1. PRC (Partial Route Calculation，部分路由计算)": "1. PRC (Partial Route Calculation)",
  "核心定义": "Core Definition",
  "：当网络上路由发生变化时，": ": When routes change on the network,",
  "只对发生变化的路由进行重新计算": "only the changed routes are recalculated",
  "，而不是重算整棵拓扑树。": ", instead of recalculating the entire topology tree.",
  "SPT 与叶子的无依赖关系处理法则": "Handling Rules for SPT and Leaf Independence",
  "SPT 变化": "SPT changes",
  "：PRC 处理变化节点上的所有叶子的路由信息。": ": PRC processes route information for all leaves on the changed node.",
  "SPT 没有变化": "SPT does not change",
  "：PRC 不会处理节点的拓扑路由信息。": ": PRC does not process the node's topological route information.",
  "叶子变化": "Leaf changes",
  "：PRC 处理变化的叶子的路由信息。": ": PRC processes route information for the changed leaves.",
  "叶子没有变化": "Leaf does not change",
  "：PRC 不会处理叶子的路由信息。": ": PRC does not process leaf route information.",
  "典型业务场景": "Typical Business Scenario",
  "：\n某路由器使能了一个新的 OSPF 业务接口（或修改了 Loopback 地址），整个网络拓扑的骨架 SPT 完全未变。此时 PRC 仅更新该节点的接口路由，完全不重算全网 SPT，节省系统资源。": ":\nA router enables a new OSPF service interface (or modifies a Loopback address), and the backbone SPT of the entire network topology remains completely unchanged. In this case, PRC only updates the interface routes for that node, without recalculating the network-wide SPT, saving system resources.",
  "2. iSPF (Incremental SPF，增量 SPF 计算)": "2. iSPF (Incremental SPF)",
  "：当网络拓扑发生结构性改变（如链路断开、新增中继路由器）时，仅对": ": When a structural change occurs in the network topology (such as a link failure or the addition of a relay router), only the",
  "受到影响的节点及其子树": "affected nodes and their subtrees",
  "进行增量重算，未受影响的树枝保持不变。": "are incrementally recalculated, while unaffected branches remain unchanged.",
  "华为实现说明": "Huawei Implementation Note",
  "：在华为主流设备（VRP5/VRP8）中，OSPF 底层默认集成了 iSPF，与 PRC 协同工作，无需手动使能。": ": In mainstream Huawei devices (VRP5/VRP8), OSPF natively integrates iSPF by default, working in coordination with PRC without the need for manual enablement.",
  "三、 控制平面节流：三大智能定时器 (Intelligent Timer)": "III. Control Plane Throttling: Three Intelligent Timers",
  "在不稳定网络中，频繁产生的振荡 LSA 会驱动路由器反复进行路由计算，导致 CPU 资源耗尽。\nOSPF 智能定时器使用**指数衰减（Exponential Backoffs）**技术，时间精度达到毫秒级。它分别对": "In unstable networks, frequently generated oscillating LSAs drive routers to perform repeated route calculations, leading to CPU resource exhaustion.\nOSPF intelligent timers use **Exponential Backoffs** technology with millisecond-level precision. They are applied respectively to",
